{"type":"standard","title":"Beth Macy","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Beth Macy</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q32860509","titles":{"canonical":"Beth_Macy","normalized":"Beth Macy","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Beth Macy</span></span>"},"pageid":56788700,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Beth_Macy.jpg/330px-Beth_Macy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":441},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ac/Beth_Macy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1543,"height":2060},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1371368962","tid":"81cb122f-a0fb-11f1-ba5b-2f7f6268e978","timestamp":"2026-08-26T03:09:10Z","description":"American journalist and writer","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beth_Macy","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beth_Macy?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beth_Macy?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Beth_Macy"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beth_Macy","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Beth_Macy","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beth_Macy?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Beth_Macy"}},"extract":"Beth Macy is an American journalist and non-fiction writer. She is the author of five books including the four national bestsellers Factory Man (2014), Truevine (2016), Dopesick (2018) and Paper Girl (2025). Macy is a Democratic candidate for Virginia's 6th congressional district in 2026.","extract_html":"<p><b>Beth Macy</b> is an American journalist and non-fiction writer. She is the author of five books including the four national bestsellers <i>Factory Man</i> (2014), <i>Truevine</i> (2016), <span><i>Dopesick</i></span> (2018) and <i>Paper Girl</i> (2025). Macy is a Democratic candidate for Virginia's 6th congressional district in 2026.</p>"}